    "findings": [
      {
        "slideId": "intake-p2",
        "blockId": null,
        "severity": "error",
        "problem": "The deck is only two slides against a six-slide brief. It gives the time result and names the unmeasured quality/error rates, but it never explains why that gap matters for the extend/stop decision or what evidence would resolve it. The audience is left with a result and a caveat, not a decision case.",
        "correction": "Add the missing decision-framing sequence: explain why unmeasured quality/error rates mean the 40→16 hour saving cannot by itself justify extension, and what evidence would be needed. The outline planner should add the remaining slides; do not compress this into p2.",
        "route": "plan"
      },
      {
        "slideId": "intake-p2",
        "blockId": null,
        "severity": "advice",
        "problem": "The chart labels the metric twice—\"Median review time, hours\" and \"Median (hours)\"—while the headline says only \"Review time fell.\" The duplicate header adds clutter, and the headline drops the median qualifier that the chart is based on.",
        "correction": "Make the headline \"Median review time fell from 40 to 16 hours [1]\" and keep one chart label (e.g., \"Median review time, hours [1]\"), removing the redundant \"Median (hours)\" header.",
        "route": "write"
      },
      {
        "slideId": "intake-p2",
        "blockId": "b2",
        "severity": "advice",
        "problem": "The bar chart keeps table-like scaffolding: the vertical gridlines are visible only in the gap between the two bars and have no tick values, so they read as column dividers rather than a scale. The row labels and hour labels also sit about 30px above their bars instead of centered, so the bars look detached from their labels.",
        "correction": "Remove the unlabeled gridlines and vertically center \"Before\"/\"During the pilot\" and the hour labels with their bars; the direct value labels already give the scale.",
        "route": "layout"
      }
    ],
